eY(7px);\"></div> <div style=\"background-color: #F4F4F4; height: 12.5px; transform: rotate(-45deg) translateX(3px) translateY(1px); width: 12.5px; flex-grow: 0; margin-right: 14px; margin-left: 2px;\"></div> <div style=\"background-color: #F4F4F4; border-radius: 50%; height: 12.5px; width: 12.5px; transform: translateX(9px) translateY(-18px);\"></div></div><div style=\"margin-left: 8px;\"> <div style=\" background-color: #F4F4F4; border-radius: 50%; flex-grow: 0; height: 20px; width: 20px;\"></div> <div style=\" width: 0; height: 0; border-top: 2px solid transparent; border-left: 6px solid #f4f4f4; border-bottom: 2px solid transparent; transform: translateX(16px) translateY(-4px) rotate(30deg)\"></div></div><div style=\"margin-left: auto;\"> <div style=\" width: 0px; border-top: 8px solid #F4F4F4; border-right: 8px solid transparent; transform: translateY(16px);\"></div> <div style=\" background-color: #F4F4F4; flex-grow: 0; height: 12px; width: 16px; transform: translateY(-4px);\"></div> <div style=\" width: 0; height: 0; border-top: 8px solid #F4F4F4; border-left: 8px solid transparent; transform: translateY(-4px) translateX(8px);\"></div></div></div> <div style=\"display: flex; flex-direction: column; flex-grow: 1; justify-content: center; margin-bottom: 24px;\"> <div style=\" background-color: #F4F4F4; border-radius: 4px; flex-grow: 0; height: 14px; margin-bottom: 6px; width: 224px;\"></div> <div style=\" background-color: #F4F4F4; border-radius: 4px; flex-grow: 0; height: 14px; width: 144px;\"></div></div></a><p style=\" color:#c9c8cd; font-family:Arial,sans-serif; font-size:14px; line-height:17px; margin-bottom:0; margin-top:8px; overflow:hidden; padding:8px 0 7px; text-align:center; text-overflow:ellipsis; white-space:nowrap;\"><a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/p/DeXTPWUii0c/?utm_source=ig_embed&amp;utm_campaign=loading\" style=\" color:#c9c8cd; font-family:Arial,sans-serif; font-size:14px; font-style:normal; font-weight:normal; line-height:17px; text-decoration:none;\" target=\"_blank\">A post shared by Ayla Aksu Kahraman (@aylaaksu6)</a></p></div></blockquote>\r\n<script async src=\"//www.instagram.com/embed.js\"></script></aside>\n</div><h4><strong>Other notable rankings movements</strong></h4>\n<p><strong>Tatjana Maria, +13 to No. 71 and Madison Brengle, +20 to No. 188: </strong>Maria, 39, and Brengle, 36, first played each other in Wimbledon qualifying in 2009. They met for a seventh time in the Templeton W100 final two weeks ago, with Maria winning for a sixth time in their rivalry 6-3, 6-4. Brengle, who followed her Templeton run by making the Lexington W50 semifinals last week, returns to the Top 200 for the first time since March 2024.</p>\n<p><strong>Ane Mintegi Del Olmo, +32 to No. 206: </strong>The 2021 Wimbledon junior champion has hit her stride in the pros this year. Mintegi Del Olmo is on a 10-match winning streak after collecting back-to-back Bulgarian W50 titles in Plovdiv and Burgas, and the 22-year-old Spaniard is up to a new career high.</p>\n<p><strong>Gao Xinyu, +24 to No. 220: </strong>The Chinese 28-year-old won her first tour-level match since the 2025 United Cup in Beijing last week -- and the first of her career on home soil -- upsetting Panna Udvardy in the Beijing first round.</p>\n<p><strong>Britt Du Pree, +40 to No. 281:</strong> The 19-year-old Dutchwoman makes her Top 300 debut after winning the Reims W35 title two weeks ago.</p>\n<p><strong>Alisa Oktiabreva, +125 to No. 311: </strong>Roland Garros junior champion Oktiabreva is on a 15-match winning streak after picking up three straight World Tennis titles -- two W35s in Santa Margherita di Pula, then last week's Heraklion W50. The 18-year-old Czech reached a career high of No. 280 this April.</p>\n<p><strong>Alena Kovackova, +67 to No. 340: </strong>Another 18-year-old Czech, Kovackova is up to a new career high after reaching the Santa Margherita di Pula W35 final (losing to Oktiabreva) and Burgas W50 semifinals.</p>\n<p><strong>Charo Esquiva Banuls, +95 to No. 449: </strong>Former junior No. 9 Esquiva Banuls is on a 10-match winning streak. The 18-year-old Spaniard won the first two professional titles of her career at the Yecla W50 and Baza W35 on home soil, and makes her Top 500 debut.</p>\n<p><strong>Astra Sharma, +605 to No. 576: </strong>After being sidelined for six months, former No. 84 Sharma returned to action in July, losing her first four matches back. But the 31-year-old Australian's comeback hit its stride over the last two weeks as she claimed the Nashville W15 and Lexington W50 titles back-to-back, the latter as a qualifier.</p>\n<p><strong>Giulia Safina Popa, +166 to No. 620: </strong>The 16-year-old Romanian compiled a 17-match winning streak over the past month, collecting three straight W15 titles in Campulung, Constanta and Varna before qualifying for the Burgas W50 last week. Popa, who qualified for her first WTA main draw as a 15-year-old last year in Iasi, is up to a new career high.</p>\n<p><strong>Ekaterina Dotsenko, +416 to No. 807: </strong>Dotsenko, the junior No. 21, has enjoyed an impressive start to her pro career. On her pro debut in July as a 14-year-old, she made a W15 final in Monastir; in her second and third events last month, she swept back-to-back W15 titles in the same venue, becoming the first 2011-born player to win a professional tournament. Dotsenko, who turned 15 years old last week, now becomes the first 2011-born player to reach the Top 1,000.</p>","author":"Alex Macpherson","subtitle":null,"summary":"Beijing champion Zheng Qinwen returns to the Top 30 in the latest edition of the PIF WTA Rankings, while finalist Mirra Andreeva becomes the youngest player to make her Top 3 debut in 21 years. Elsewhere, Nikola Bartunkova, Alina Charaeva and Sun Xinran all hit significant milestones after making an impact in Beijing.","hotlinkUrl":null,"duration":525,"contentSummary":null,"leadMedia":{"id":4590906,"accountId":29,"type":"photo","title":"Zheng Qinwen, Beijing 2026","description":null,"date":"2026-10-12T10:06:00Z","location":null,"coordinates":[0.0,0.0],"commentsOn":false,"copyright":null,"publishFrom":1791799599896,"publishTo":0,"tags":[],"platform":"PULSE_CMS","language":"en","additionalInfo":{},"canonicalUrl":"","references":[{"label":null,"id":328120,"type":"TENNIS_PLAYER","sid":"328120"},{"label":null,"id":1020,"type":"TENNIS_TOURNAMENTGROUP","sid":"1020"}],"related":[],"metadata":{"credit":"Pedro Pardo/AFP via Getty Images"},"titleTranslations":null,"lastModified":1791799629904,"titleUrlSegment":"zheng-f-pedro-pardo","visibilityOrder":[],"allowedUserGroups":[],"allowedTerritories":[],"subtitle":null,"onDemandUrl":"https://photoresources.wtatennis.com/photo-resources/2026/10/12/fac89aec-33fc-459c-af9c-aa85256fe85e/Zheng-F-Pedro-Pardo.jpg","originalDetails":{"width":4383,"height":3005,"aspectRatio":1.458569},"imageUrl":"https://photoresources.wtatennis.com/wta/photo/2026/10/12/081c6e7c-e47c-49bf-b4d5-6cba944513c9/Zheng-F-Pedro-Pardo.jpg"},"imageUrl":"https://photoresources.wtatennis.com/wta/photo/2026/10/12/081c6e7c-e47c-49bf-b4d5-6cba944513c9/Zheng-F-Pedro-Pardo.jpg","onDemandUrl":"https://photoresources.wtatennis.com/photo-resources/2026/10/12/fac89aec-33fc-459c-af9c-aa85256fe85e/Zheng-F-Pedro-Pardo.jpg"}